.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.zip
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Sweep outputs ARE committed. The Kaggle notebook pushes results/ to GitHub
# after every run because a session that dies otherwise loses everything — one
# n=750 sweep was already lost that way (PROGRESS.md, 2026-07-29). `results/`
# used to be ignored wholesale and every push needed `git add -f`, which meant a
# plain `git add -A` silently skipped new results. Ignore only the dev-seed
# scratch files instead; SPEC's seed hygiene keeps seeds 0 and 1234 out of the
# experiment, so nothing ignored here is ever reportable.
results/*_seed0.*
results/*_seed1234.*
results/smoke_*
